{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_6d0a3b3f5ecf",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 7266,
      "mechanism": "During non-FRAME_FIFO mode (FRAME_FIFO=1 so this path is not taken in this config, but the gate change introduces a static !full_cur qualification on the non-FRAME_FIFO branch), the early return would block the write path entirely when full_cur is asserted, preventing the consumer from ever advancing rd_ptr and clearing space. The observed m_axis_tvalid=1 at cycles 13-15 while expected 0 suggests the FIFO continued emitting data it should not have; gating on !full_cur in the wrong branch corrupts the handshake sequencing."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_cac4f5704d7e",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 7595,
      "mechanism": "The edit changes the frame-close condition from plain s_axis_tlast to (s_axis_tlast && !full_wr). When full_wr is asserted (write pointer about to wrap into commit pointer), the frame is prevented from committing even if s_axis_tlast arrives, so wr_ptr is not advanced to wr_ptr_cur and the frame remains uncommitted. The consumer then never receives that frame, but stale data from a previous committed frame stays in m_axis_reg, causing m_axis_tvalid to remain 1 when it should drop to 0."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_fb20f7054af1",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 5768,
      "mechanism": "Replaces the USER_ENABLE gate in the generate block with (USER_ENABLE && !s_axis_tvalid). This widens the s_axis_tuser assignment to be conditional on !s_axis_tvalid, effectively breaking the packing of USER_WIDTH into the s_axis bus whenever s_axis_tvalid=1. The downstream m_axis_tuser (and thus frame qualification) receives garbage, making the frame-drop logic misbehave and leaving m_axis_tvalid spuriously high."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_a1b8a0260a9f",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 7193,
      "mechanism": "Changes the entry guard to (s_axis_tready && s_axis_tvalid && !drop_frame_reg). When drop_frame_reg=1 (we are mid-frame overflow), the gate blocks all further s_axis_tvalid processing, including the s_axis_tlast that should terminate the overflow and clear drop_frame_reg. The FIFO then never recovers from drop_frame_reg, never commits new frames, and m_axis_tvalid stays asserted on old data."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_c283d27d2530",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 7054,
      "mechanism": "Replaces the constant 1'b0 default for overflow_next with overflow_reg, making overflow a sticky latch. Once overflow_reg=1 it never clears, so status_overflow stays 1 and the write-side logic (full_cur/full_wr) permanently sees an overflow condition, suppressing frame commits and causing m_axis_tvalid to hold stale data."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_33eda120828e",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 7193,
      "mechanism": "Replaces the entry guard with (s_axis_tready && s_axis_tvalid && full_wr). This only allows writes when full_wr is asserted, i.e., when the write pointer is about to collide with the commit pointer. Normal operation (plenty of space) has full_wr=0, so all writes are blocked, the FIFO stays empty, and m_axis_tvalid incorrectly holds its previous value instead of going to 0."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_ad9c3f237cc3",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 5846,
      "mechanism": "In the generate block, USER_ENABLE becomes (USER_ENABLE && s_axis_tready). This makes the s_axis_tuser packing dependent on s_axis_tready, corrupting the user field whenever backpressure applies. The frame-drop decision (USER_BAD_FRAME_MASK & ~(s_axis_tuser ^ USER_BAD_FRAME_VALUE)) then sees wrong user bits, misclassifying frames and leaving m_axis_tvalid asserted on a frame that should have been dropped."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_87e9f03179c2",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 7266,
      "mechanism": "In the non-FRAME_FIFO branch, replaces !FRAME_FIFO with (!FRAME_FIFO && full_cur). Since FRAME_FIFO=1 in this configuration, this branch is never taken, but the edit introduces a static full_cur qualification that would invert the write enable for a non-frame FIFO, breaking the consumer handshake and indirectly causing m_axis_tvalid to mismatch in any mode-switch scenario."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "The discovery trace shows m_axis_tvalid=1 at cycles 13-15 when the oracle expects 0, indicating the FIFO emitted data it should have suppressed. The top-ranked patches directly corrupt the write-side frame-commit handshake (frame-close gating, drop-frame recovery, overflow stickiness) or the input-packing logic that feeds the frame-drop decision, all of which can leave m_axis_reg holding a stale committed frame. Lower-ranked patches introduce spurious qualifications on branches not taken in this configuration or on generate-block packing, which indirectly poison frame metadata. Each cited line and port come from the supplied candidate list and the public discovery trace."
}
